--TEST--
`Core\Request::post` answers the same way for every name it is given when no request arrived, so nothing about the field reaches the decision -- ADR 0012 § 7, ADR 0105 § 2, spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Invariance over a sweep, counted rather than read off a line. `post` reads a
// *body*, and a body is the one thing about a request a program is most likely
// to have decided is simply empty -- so a member that reported "no such field"
// for one spelling and refused for another would be telling a caller something
// about a form that does not exist. Whether a request arrived is decided before
// the name is looked at.
uint $refused = 0;
try {
    Core\Request::post("title");
} catch (LogicError $ordinary) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::post("");
} catch (LogicError $empty) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
// ADR 0105 § 2 gives `post` the bracket convention `query` reads, so a nested
// key is the spelling most able to take a different path through the parse --
// and it must not reach one, the parse being downstream of this refusal.
try {
    Core\Request::post("a[b]");
} catch (LogicError $bracketed) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
try {
    Core\Request::post("a field with spaces and %20 in it");
} catch (LogicError $unspellable) {
    $refused = $refused + 1;
}
echo "every name refused: ", $refused, " of 4\n";

// The message is the same one for all four, which is the counted claim stated
// the other way: it names the member and never the name, so no spelling of a
// field can be told apart from another by reading it.
try {
    Core\Request::post("a[b]");
} catch (LogicError $why) {
    echo $why->message, "\n";
}

// And a program reaches the line after five refusals: ADR 0020 § 1's ladder,
// not a fatal.
echo "still running\n";
--EXPECT--
every name refused: 4 of 4
Core\Request::post(): there is no request here — this program is not answering one, as a CLI program, a scheduled script, a job worker and a test are not. That is refused rather than answered empty, because "no request arrived" and "the request sent nothing" are different facts
still running
